        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-02T16:56:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Where is this gsh_buffdesc coming from? Honestly, I have been starting to wonder if we should stop using gsh_buffdesc for strings, so at the earliest time we create NUL terminated strings that get passed around.\n\nI\u0027m not opposed to merging this, it would just be nice to avoid muddy waters.\n\nOptionally I guess we assume gsh_buffdesc is never NUL terminated and make copies all over the place...",
      "parentUuid": "f3054aa9_5100bb49",
      "revId": "e8e95e47e76ea2f12ad25cf05639ec9c522520a5",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d1b31f9_b1bade99",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-03T08:15:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The callers to this function are-\n`decode_acl`, `decode_owner`, `decode_group`\n\nThey\u0027re not allocating memory, but just pointing to the XDR received buffer that was received from the client",
      "parentUuid": "23eac52b_b61b3b5d",
      "revId": "e8e95e47e76ea2f12ad25cf05639ec9c522520a5",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70458fe9_5c8c51ab",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-03T16:34:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, OK, so decode_acl provides a large enough buffer to inline_xdr_utf8string which NUL terminates the string.\n\nI do see that decode_owner and decode_group do not. Let\u0027s actually fix them so they conform to the expectation that strings in gsh_buffdesc are actually NUL terminated (which they ARE supposed to be - I just didn\u0027t catch those two places...).",
      "parentUuid": "1d1b31f9_b1bade99",
      "revId": "e8e95e47e76ea2f12ad25cf05639ec9c522520a5",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4acbec2d_67b1bec4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-04T11:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we want to allocate memory in those functions and trust the callees later on to release it?\n\nSounds a bit error prone to me, also it isn\u0027t used in all code paths",
      "parentUuid": "70458fe9_5c8c51ab",
      "revId": "e8e95e47e76ea2f12ad25cf05639ec9c522520a5",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f852e1c8_20941dc9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-04T15:00:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Memory doesn\u0027t need to be allocated, the string is only needed to convert the XDR param to a uid or gid. So an alloca or a local char[x] buffer is sufficient. See how decode_acl works, no reason for decode_owner and decode_group to work the same way.\n\nReally the solution would be to not use gsh_buffdesc to pass strings. Then, closer to where the string came from we resolve NUL termination and the expectation of NUL terminated string is more clear in the API.",
      "parentUuid": "4acbec2d_67b1bec4",
      "revId": "e8e95e47e76ea2f12ad25cf05639ec9c522520a5",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
